#: ../../../doc-guide/parse-headers.rst:80
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../doc-guide/parse-headers.rst:82
msgid ""
"Creates an enriched version of a Kernel header file with cross-links to each "
"C data structure type, from ``FILE_IN``, formatting it with reStructuredText "
"notation, either as-is or as a table of contents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../doc-guide/parse-headers.rst:86
msgid ""
"It accepts an optional ``FILE_RULES`` which describes what elements will be "
"either ignored or be pointed to a non-default reference, and optionally "
"defines the C namespace to be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../doc-guide/parse-headers.rst:90
msgid ""
"It is meant to allow having more comprehensive documentation, where uAPI "
"headers will create cross-reference links to the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../doc-guide/parse-headers.rst:93
msgid "The output is written at the ``FILE_OUT``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../doc-guide/parse-headers.rst:95
msgid ""
"The ``FILE_RULES`` may contain contain three types of statements: "
"**ignore**, **replace** and **namespace**."
msgstr ""

